  "title": "Voice Is the Final Interface: The World of 'Her' Is Becoming Real",
  "summary": "In Spike Jonze's Her, everyone walks through the city talking quietly to an AI, each in their own bubble, and no one thinks it strange. As artificial intelligence grows capable enough to do the actual work, that calm, screen-free, voice-first world stops being science fiction. Here is why voice is the final interface, what the movie's world gets right, and how VoiceOS is building toward it.",
